{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310580,"nonce":"y/pez5ucWCoL5obBDsEJOV2jx28=","title":"OPEN general bug — a non-zero trailing DEFAULT-VALUE arg on an instance method is filled with ZERO at the call site (func_id drift + ...","message":"**OPEN, general, HIGH.** A method with a trailing **default-value** param (`b:Int = -1`) called WITHOUT that arg gets the param filled with **type-zero (0), not the declared default (-1)**. Silent wrong value, no error. Reproduces **same-file** (not just x-module):\n\n```haxe\nclass Box { public function pick(a:Int, b:Int = -1):Int { return b \u003c 0 ? a+100 : b; } }\n// box.pick(5, 7) =\u003e 7  OK ;  box.pick(5) =\u003e 0  WRONG (expected 105)\n```\n\nZero-defaults (`from:Int = 0`) work by accident (zero-fill == the default), so the bug only bites **non-zero** defaults. This is DISTINCT from [[bugs_optional_arg_unfilled_garbage_abi_slot]] (that was `?opt` on instance dispatch skipping fill_default_args, FIXED) — here fill_default_args RUNS but can't find the defaults.\n\n**Root cause (diagnosed via RZT_DBG_DEFARG probe in hir_to_mir.rs):** `fill_default_args` (hir_to_mir.rs:23399) looks up `function_param_defaults` keyed by `func_id`; on miss it **zero-fills by signature type** (the `IrValue::I32(0)` fallback, ~23466). The lookup misses because:\n1. **func_id DRIFT** — the definition inserts pick's defaults under `func_id=2` (its canonical body id, insert at hir_to_mir.rs:3197/3311), but the CALL SITE (fill at 18060, has_implicit_this) resolves pick to a large synthesized id that even DIFFERS per call: `160004` for `pick(5)`, `220004` for `pick(5,7)`. Same method, same file, 3 different ids. Keying defaults by that drift-prone id can never match.\n2. **ordering** — `main` (caller) is lowered while `function_param_defaults` is still empty (probe: `map_len=0` at the pick calls), before pick's body/defaults are registered.\n\n**Durable fix = resolve defaults by NAME/symbol, not func_id** (matches the whole x-module cluster guidance [[bugs_interface_dispatch_symbolid_drift_fix]], [[bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster]]) + a PRE-PASS that registers all param defaults before any body is lowered (so order doesn't matter). Both needed; keying by the synthesized call-site id alone won't work. Moderate, touches the sensitive x-module resolution path — treat as its own session; user should greenlight.\n\n**Workaround in use:** avoid default args entirely. [[project_slice_zero_copy_string_view]] (rayzor.Slice) ships an explicit-arg API (`slice(a,b)`/`tail(a)`/`sub(a,n)`) for exactly this reason — no defaults ⇒ fill_default_args has nothing to fill ⇒ bug can't manifest.\n\nAlso seen alongside: **StringBuf.add(x) renders `\u003cunknown type N\u003e` for plain String** — separate known issue (add takes Dynamic; String→Dynamic UNSAFE, see [[bugs_cross_module_dynamic_object_reflection]]). Use `+`/`+=` concat, not StringBuf.add, in repros.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_default_arg_nonzero_funcid_drift` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}